{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-1","title":"Ezekiel 14:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God answers idolaters according to their own heart. 6 They are exhorted to repent, for fear of judgments, by means of seduced prophets. 12 God's irrevocable sentence of famine; 15 of noisome beasts; 17 of the sword; 19 and of pestilence. 22 A remnant shall be reserved for example of others.</p>\n<p>certain. 8:1; 20:1; 2Ki 6:32; Ac 4:5,8 and sat. 33:31; Isa 29:13; Lu 10:39; Ac 22:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-2","title":"Ezekiel 14:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>1Ki 14:4; Am 3:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-3","title":"Ezekiel 14:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>these men. 4,7; 6:9; 11:21; 20:16; 36:25; Jer 17:1,2,9; Eph 5:5 and put. 3:20; 7:19; 44:12; Jer 44:16-18; Zep 1:3; 1Pe 2:8; Re 2:14 should. 20:3; 1Sa 28:6; 2Ki 3:13; Ps 66:18; 101:3; Pr 15:8,29; 21:27; 28:9 Isa 1:15; 33:15; Jer 7:8-11; 11:11; 42:20,21; Zec 7:13; Lu 20:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-4","title":"Ezekiel 14:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>speak. 2:7; 3:4,17-21 I the Lord. 7; 1Ki 21:20-25; 2Ki 1:16; Isa 3:11; 66:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-5","title":"Ezekiel 14:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>I may. 9,10; Ho 10:2; Zec 7:11-14; 2Th 2:9-11 estranged. De 32:15,16; Isa 1:4; *marg: Jer 2:5,11-13,31,32; Zec 11:8; Ro 1:21-23,28,30; 8:7; Ga 6:7 Eph 4:18; Col 1:21; Heb 3:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-6","title":"Ezekiel 14:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>Repent. 18:30; 1Sa 7:3; 1Ki 8:47-49; Ne 1:8,9; Isa 55:6,7; Jer 8:5,6 Jer 31:18-20; 50:4,5; La 3:39-41; Ho 14:1-3,8; Jon 3:7-9 Mt 3:8-10; Ac 3:19; 17:30; 26:20; Jas 4:8-10 yourselves. or, others. turn. 4; 8:16; 16:63; 36:31,32; 2Ch 29:6; Isa 2:20; 30:22; Jer 13:27 Zep 3:11; Ro 6:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-7","title":"Ezekiel 14:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>of the stranger. Ex 12:48; 20:10; Le 16:29; 20:2; 24:22; Nu 15:15,29 separateth. Ho 4:14; 9:10; Jude 1:19 and setteth. 3,4 and cometh. 33:30-32; 2Ki 8:8-15; Isa 58:1,2; Jer 21:1,2; 37:1-3,9,10,17 Jer 38:14-23 by. 4,7,8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-8","title":"Ezekiel 14:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>I will set. 15:7; Le 17:10; 20:3-6; 26:17; Ps 34:16; Jer 21:10; 44:11 a sign. 5:15; Nu 26:10; De 28:37; Ps 37:22; 44:13,14; Isa 65:15; Jer 24:9 Jer 29:22 I will cut. Le 20:3; 22:3; Nu 19:20; Ro 11:22; 1Co 10:11 and ye. 6:7; 13:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-9","title":"Ezekiel 14:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>if the. 20:25; 2Sa 12:11,12; 1Ki 22:20-23; Job 12:16; Ps 81:11,12 Isa 63:16; 66:4; Jer 4:10; 2Th 2:9-12 I the.That is, I have suffered him to be deceived; I have given him up to \"strong delusions to believe a lie,\" as a just judgment upon him for going after idols, and setting up false pretensions to inspiration. God, according to the genius of the Hebrew language, is often said to do a thing, which he only suffers, or permits.</p>\n<p>and I will. 16:27; Isa 5:25; 9:12,17,21; 10:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-10","title":"Ezekiel 14:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>they shall. 17:18-20; 23:49; Ge 4:13; Nu 5:31; Mic 7:9; Ga 6:5 the punishment. 4,7,8; De 13:1-10; 17:2-7; Jer 6:14,15; 8:11,12; 14:15; Re 19:19-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-11","title":"Ezekiel 14:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>the house. 34:10-31; 44:10,15; 48:11; De 13:11; 19:20; Ps 119:67; Isa 9:16 Jer 23:15; 50:6; 2Pe 2:15 neither. 11:18-20; 36:25-29; 37:23 that they. 34:30; 36:28; 37:27; 39:22; Ge 17:7; Jer 11:4; 31:33; 32:38; Zec 13:9 Heb 8:10; 11:16; Re 21:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-13","title":"Ezekiel 14:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>when. 9:9; Ezr 9:6; Isa 24:20; La 1:8,20; Da 9:5,10-12 break. 4:16; 5:16; Le 26:26; Isa 3:1; Jer 15:2,3; La 4:9,10 and will cut. 17,19,21; 25:13; Ge 6:7; Jer 7:20; 32:43; 36:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-14","title":"Ezekiel 14:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>these. 16,18,20 Noah. Ge 6:8; 7:1; 8:20,21; Heb 11:7 Daniel. 28:3; Da 9:21; 10:11 Job. Job 1:5; 42:8,9; Jer 7:16; 11:14; 14:11,12; 15:1 deliver. 20; Pr 11:4; 2Pe 2:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-15","title":"Ezekiel 14:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>noisome. 5:17; Le 26:22; 1Ki 20:36; 2Ki 17:25; Jer 15:3 spoil. or, bereave.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-16","title":"Ezekiel 14:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>these. 14,18; Mt 18:19,20; Jas 5:16 in it. Heb. in the midst of it. as I live. 20; 33:11; Nu 14:28,29 they shall. Ge 18:23-33; 19:29; Job 22:20; Ac 27:24; Heb 11:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-17","title":"Ezekiel 14:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>I bring. 5:12,17; 21:3,4,9-15; 29:8; 38:21,22; Le 26:25; Jer 25:9; 47:6 so that. 13; 25:13; Jer 33:12; Ho 4:3; Zep 1:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-19","title":"Ezekiel 14:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>if I. 5:12; 38:22; Nu 14:12; 16:46-50; De 28:21,22,59-61; 2Sa 24:13,15 1Ki 8:37; 2Ch 6:28; 7:13; 20:9; Ps 91:3,6; Isa 37:36; Jer 14:12 Jer 21:6,9; 24:10; Am 4:10; Mt 24:7 and pour. 7:8; 36:18; Re 16:3-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-20","title":"Ezekiel 14:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>Noah. 14,16 Daniel.Daniel, says Abp. Newcombe, was \"taken captive in the third year of Jehoiakim, (Da 1:1.) After this, Jehoiakam reigned eight years, (2 Ki 23:36.) And this prophecy, as appears from ch. 8:1, was uttered in the sixth year of Jehoiachin's captivity, who succeeded Jehoiakim, and reigned only three months, (2 Ki 24:6, 8.) Therefore, at this time, Daniel had been fourteen years in captivity;\" and was, as is generally supposed, about thirty years of age.</p>\n<p>by. 18:20,22; Job 5:19-24; Ps 33:18,19; Isa 3:10; Ho 10:12; Zep 2:3 Ac 10:35; 1Jo 2:29; 3:7,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-21","title":"Ezekiel 14:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>How much more when. or, Also when. my four. 13,15,17,19; 5:12,17; 6:11,12; 33:27; Jer 15:2,3; Am 4:6-12 Re 6:4-8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-22","title":"Ezekiel 14:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>behold, therein. 6:8; De 4:31; 2Ch 36:20; Isa 6:13; 10:20-22; 17:4-6; 24:13; 40:1,2 Isa 65:8,9; Jer 4:27; 5:19; 30:11; 52:27-30; Mic 5:7; Mr 13:20 Heb 12:6-11 ye shall see. 6:9,10; 16:63; 20:43; 36:31; Jer 31:17-21 ye shall be. Jer 3:21-25</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-14-23","title":"Ezekiel 14:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":14,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":14,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>that I have not. 8:6-18; 9:8,9; Ge 18:22-33; De 8:2; Ne 9:33; Pr 26:2; Jer 7:17-28 Jer 22:8,9; Da 9:7,14; Ro 2:5; Re 15:4; 16:6</p>"}]}